# 12-Column Grid Layout

Page and section structure uses a **12-column CSS Grid**. Flexbox is only for small inner positioning.

`Container` (and `Section`) is the grid: `grid-cols-12`. Direct children **span columns** — they do not start a second layout model.

## Spans

| Role | Classes |
|------|---------|
| Full width | `col-span-12` |
| Half | `col-span-12 md:col-span-6` |
| Third | `col-span-12 md:col-span-4` |
| Two thirds | `col-span-12 md:col-span-8` |
| Quarter (stats) | `col-span-6 md:col-span-3` |

```js
// ❌ BAD — nested 2-col grid instead of spanning the page grid
<Section>
  <div className="grid md:grid-cols-2">...</div>
</Section>

// ✅ GOOD — children participate in the 12-column Container
<Section>
  <div className="col-span-12 md:col-span-6">...</div>
  <div className="col-span-12 md:col-span-6">...</div>
</Section>
```

## Flex only in small components

Use Flex for positioning **inside** a grid cell: icon + label, button groups, Clerk controls, checkbox rows.

```js
// ✅ OK — flex for alignment inside one cell
<div className="col-span-12 md:col-span-6">
  <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
    <Button>Explore</Button>
    <Button>Start</Button>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Avoid

- `flex` / `flex-wrap` / `sm:flex-row` for section or page columns
- `grid-cols-2` / `grid-cols-3` on section wrappers (use `col-span-*` on the 12-col parent)
- Overriding `Container` with another `grid-cols-*`
- `flex-1` for page chrome — use `grid-rows-[auto_1fr_auto]` on the app shell

## Checklist

- [ ] Section content is direct `col-span-*` children of `Section` / `Container`
- [ ] Halves / thirds / quarters use the span table above
- [ ] Flex appears only in molecules/atoms for alignment
